From f6ee84f55bb7c00f854e31aa0ed25ed1e9ec15e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alberto Miranda <alberto.miranda@seqera.io>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:15:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] x86: make PAGE_SIZE unsigned long on musl

musl's <limits.h> defines PAGE_SIZE as a plain int (4096). It wins over
our (1UL << PAGE_SHIFT), which is only set under #ifndef PAGE_SIZE. Any
nr * PAGE_SIZE with an int nr then overflows once nr reaches 524288
pages (2 GiB).

Restore hits this with incremental pre-dumps: pages unchanged since the
parent dump coalesce into one long in-parent pagemap entry, read in one
call. For a 715080-page region, restore_priv_vma_content() does
va += nr * PAGE_SIZE, which lands exactly 4 GiB short:

  Error (criu/mem.c): Page entry address 7f20ced02000 outside of VMA
  7f21203ba000-7f21ced02000

read_parent_page() and read_pagemap_page() have the same pattern.
Commit 053a22a23 ("pagemap: prevent integer overflow in pagemap_len")
fixed one instance of this; fix the type instead of every call site.

A bare #undef is not enough: a <limits.h> included later redefines
PAGE_SIZE, and GCC does not warn about redefinitions inside system
headers. Include <limits.h> first so its include guard makes later
includes a no-op.

glibc does not define PAGE_SIZE, so glibc builds are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Alberto Miranda <alberto.miranda@seqera.io>
---
 include/common/arch/x86/asm/page.h | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/common/arch/x86/asm/page.h b/include/common/arch/x86/asm/page.h
index d31e82c60..7138bb71b 100644
--- a/include/common/arch/x86/asm/page.h
+++ b/include/common/arch/x86/asm/page.h
@@ -5,9 +5,14 @@
 #define PAGE_SHIFT 12
 #endif
 
-#ifndef PAGE_SIZE
+/*
+ * musl's <limits.h> defines PAGE_SIZE as a plain int, so nr * PAGE_SIZE
+ * overflows once nr reaches 2 GiB worth of pages. Pull it in first and
+ * override it: its include guard keeps later includes from undoing this.
+ */
+#include <limits.h>
+#undef PAGE_SIZE
 #define PAGE_SIZE (1UL << PAGE_SHIFT)
-#endif
 
 #ifndef PAGE_MASK
 #define PAGE_MASK (~(PAGE_SIZE - 1))
-- 
2.54.0

